{"description":"Capture a short spoken message, encode it with Opus, deliver it through the coordinator as an attachment, and play it back on receipt. Compiled only under the `voice` build tag.\n\nInteraction is a toggle — tap to start, tap to send — because a terminal does not report key-release events. Hold-to-talk is offered only where the Kitty keyboard protocol is detected, and is an enhancement rather than the primary path.\n\nNo latency requirement applies to this item at all, which is precisely why it is in the MVP and real-time calling is not.\n\nGated on spk:audio-toolchain-viability. If that spike fails, this item is canceled and the MVP ships without voice.","acceptanceCriteria":"1. A captured voice note reaches the recipient and plays back intelligibly on both linux/amd64 and linux/arm64.\n2. Capture is toggle-driven and works on a plain terminal with no key-release support.\n3. Where the Kitty keyboard protocol is detected, hold-to-talk is available; where it is not, the feature is absent without error or warning noise.\n4. A recipient running a build without the `voice` tag receives a clear indication that a voice note arrived and cannot be played locally. It is neither hidden nor treated as an error.\n5. A voice note sent to an offline device is queued and delivered on reconnect, like any other message.\n6. Recording shows a visible level indicator, so a user can tell the microphone is live before speaking."}